  ============================================================================
  Dark Roast: Copper Roast — iTerm2 Color Scheme
  Version: 5.1.0 Companion

  WHAT IS THIS
  ——————
  A complete iTerm2 color scheme (.itermcolors) implementing the Dark Roast
  design system's ANSI-16 palette. Covers all 16 ANSI colors plus every iTerm2
  chrome key (background, foreground, cursor, selection, bold, badge, tab, link).

  INSTALL
  ———-
  Option A (easiest — double-click):
    1. Double-click "Dark Roast Copper Roast.itermcolors" in Finder
       (or: open "Dark Roast Copper Roast.itermcolors" from Terminal)
    2. iTerm2 will import it automatically under Preferences →
       Profiles → Colors → Color Presets → "Dark Roast Copper Roast"
    3. Select it from the Color Presets dropdown in your profile

  Option B (manual import):
    1. iTerm2 → Settings (⌘,) → Profiles → Colors
    2. Click "Color Presets..." dropdown → "Import..."
    3. Select this file
    4. Select "Dark Roast Copper Roast" from the Color Presets dropdown

  Option C (apply to all profiles):
    Import as above, then go to each profile and select the preset.
    To set as default for new sessions, update the "Default" profile.

  ABOUT THE FORMAT
  ————————
  iTerm2 stores colors as XML plists where each color is a dict with five keys:
    Alpha Component  — float 0.0–1.0  (1.0 = fully opaque)
    Blue Component   — float 0.0–1.0
    Color Space      — string ("sRGB" for standard, "P3" for wide-gamut)
    Green Component  — float 0.0–1.0
    Red Component    — float 0.0–1.0

  All Dark Roast colors are specified in sRGB. No P3 wide-gamut is used; the
  palette is designed for warm espresso tones, not high-saturation display-P3.

  PALETTE PHILOSOPHY
  —————————
  All four Dark Roast terminal themes (Warp, Tabby, Terminal.app, iTerm2)
  share an identical ANSI-16 palette so that ls, git diff, vim syntax,
  tmux, and every other CLI tool produce exactly the same output regardless
  of which emulator you're running in.

  FULL COLOR REFERENCE
  ——————————
  Chrome:
    background    #34251C   void      — warm-dark deepest layer
    foreground    #FFF9F4   crema     — primary text (14.09:1 contrast vs void)
    cursor        #24C6B6   teal      — kinetic cursor, matches editor caret
    cursor text   #34251C   void      — text inside cursor block (inverted)
    selection bg  #47352A   espresso  — warm polished surface (v4: was `grain`)
    selection fg  #FFF9F4   crema     — text color on selection
    bold          #FFF9F4   crema     — bold text color (same hue, higher weight)
    badge         #FF7D70   scarlet   — iTerm2 badge/notification
    tab           #3A2A20   obsidian  — tab bar background color
    link          #24C6B6   teal      — hyperlink color in terminal output

  ANSI Normal (indices 0–7):
    0  black       #3A2A20   obsidian  — dark floor (not as deep as void)
    1  red         #FF7D70   scarlet   — error / critical
    2  green       #7DC45F   sage      — warm fern (terminal extension)
    3  yellow      #F5A33A   amber     — warning / accent
    4  blue        #5DB4E8   slate     — dusty steel blue (terminal extension)
    5  magenta     #DB86D0   mauve     — dried lavender (terminal extension)
    6  cyan        #24C6B6   teal      — live data flow / resolved
    7  white       #F3E7DD   bone      — reduced-contrast light text

  ANSI Bright (indices 8–15):
    8  bright black    #C4A78E   crater-deep — comment gray, tmux inactive (v4: was `crater`)
    9  bright red      #FF9184   scarlet+  — scarlet companion-bright
    10 bright green    #A3DD7B   sage+     — sage companion-bright
    11 bright yellow   #E4B20B   gold      — success / stable severity
    12 bright blue     #68D0F8   slate+    — slate companion-bright
    13 bright magenta  #EC94E0   mauve+    — mauve companion-bright
    14 bright cyan     #5FE0D1   teal+     — teal brightened (lighter than #24C6B6;
                                             bright should be visibly brighter)
    15 bright white    #FFF9F4   crema     — full brightness
  ============================================================================
-->
